    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p38.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "First \\(f(4)=4-2=2.\\) Therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} F[3,f(4)]&=F(3,2)\\\\ &=2^2+3=7. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Evaluate the inner function \\(f(4)\\) first",
        "Then substitute \\(a=3\\) and the resulting value for \\(b\\) into \\(F(a,b)\\)"
